RECONCILIATIONS (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
R1 OUTPUT PATH. The generated prompt names the output
   `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/LiveLogsPage.swift`. That directory is NOT a
   source root in `apps/apple/project.yml` (the iOS/macOS app targets compile
   `Sources/**` + `TeslaSync/{feature-views,dashboard-widgets,misc-surfaces,
   shared-surfaces,widget-primitives}` + `Localization` + the generated tokens). A file
   under `TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**` would never be compiled. EVERY sibling admin page
   (ApiLogs, AuditLog, LiveSignalInspector, FeatureFlags, …) lives in
   `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/`; the page is implemented there to match the
   built, shipping convention (identical to the ApiLogs precedent's recorded path
   reconciliation). Tests go in `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/`.

R2 STRING KEYS. Web `liveLogs.*` keys are mirrored into the platform catalog under the
   `translation.` namespace (the i18next default ns), exactly like the ApiLogs sibling.
   All 31 required strings already exist in `Localizable.xcstrings` as
   `translation.liveLogs.*` (+ the `translation.liveLogs.level.*` picker labels) —
   verified present; ZERO new string keys were needed for the 37 parity items. The catalog
   values use iOS positional format specifiers (`%1$@`), NOT `{{token}}`, so the buffered/
   received/drops captions + the download filename interpolate via `String(format:)`
   (`LiveLogsFormat.format` / `.downloadFilename`). Only the navigation title
   `route.liveLogs` (+ `spotlight.route.liveLogs.description`) was added for the new
   `AppRoute` case.

R3 ROUTE. The manifest records the web route as `(unrouted)` (LiveLogsPage is rendered ad
   hoc in the web app, not in `App.tsx` routes). The native client surfaces it as a
   first-class System-group destination — a new `.liveLogs` `AppRoute` (path segment
   `live-logs`, icon `doc.plaintext`, System group) reachable directly and via the
   `/admin/live-logs` deep-link alias, registered through `LiveLogsRouteRegistration` —
   so it is navigable + deep-linkable alongside the sibling admin pages. This is additive
   faithfulness, never scope narrowing.

R4 LIVE SSE TRANSPORT. Web `useLogStream` (fetch + ReadableStream SSE over
   `GET /admin/logs/stream`, rAF-batched, 1000-event rolling buffer) → a `LiveLogsStream`
   `AsyncStream<LiveLogFrame>` seam bound through the `@Observable LiveLogsPageModel`
   (ADR-004 — no transport in the view). The subscription is tied to the view lifecycle by
   `.task(id: model.subscriptionKey)`, which re-opens on a level/grep/reconnect change and
   tears down on disappear; PAUSE keeps the connection open and merely drops appends (web
   parity); the client-side vehicle filter never re-subscribes. The 1000-row FIFO buffer,
   `totalReceived`/`drops` counters, and the 5-state `ConnectionBadge` precedence are
   ported 1:1. Production binds the same shared SSE client the live signal store uses.

R5 STALENESS. The implementation spec requires a `>2 min` staleness indicator (ADR-013).
   Added as an amber + clock flag on the live badge, recomputed by a `TimelineView` clock
   (`LiveLogsControlsPanel.connectionBadge` → `model.isStale(now:)`), using the standard
   2-minute window (`LiveLogsLimits.stalenessWindow`, the `LiveStalenessPolicy.standard`
   contract) applied at the display boundary without the KMP-coupled connection-phase
   overload — keeping the model Foundation-only + harness-testable. Additive, no new strings.

R6 AI SUMMARY PANEL. The web page also embeds `<AILogTraceSummarization>`
   (`@/components/ai/AILogTraceSummarization`, keys `liveLogs.aiSummary.*`). That is a
   SEPARATE shared-component parity unit — it is NOT a `GlassPanel` and NONE of its
   `aiSummary.*` strings appear in this page's 4 panels / 31 strings / 37 required items
   (manifest record verified). It is therefore out of scope for THIS page unit and is not
   stubbed here; the 4 required panels (filters / controls / error / table) are reproduced
   in full.

R7 COMPOSITION ROOT. Adding `.liveLogs` to the `TeslaSyncApp` route-host chain deepened the
   pre-existing 17-level nested `.registry(base:)` expression past the 120-col budget once
   swiftformat re-wrapped it (swiftformat vs. swiftlint tension on the deep nesting). The
   chain was flattened into a single `makeRouteHosts()` builder (sequential
   `hosts = X.registry(base: hosts)`), preserving the exact registration set + ordering +
   the FleetCompare `onNavigate` / Settings `model`+`onOpenNotifications` arguments. Passes
   both tools. This is the documented registration seam, not a sibling surface.

