================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI LiveLogsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
`@Observable` `LiveLogsPageModel` (ADR-004 — no transport in the view) owning the 1000-row
rolling buffer, the server-side (level/grep) + client-side (vehicle id) filters, the pause /
auto-scroll / enabled flags, the received/drop/connection telemetry, and an ADR-013 freshness
clock — bound to a cold `LiveLogsStream` `AsyncStream` seam whose frames mirror the web SSE
taxonomy (connected/log/drop/failed), the subscription tied to the view lifecycle by
`.task(id:)`. The page reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle), the filter panel (minimum
level menu, grep field + helper text applied on submit/blur, client-side vehicle id), the
controls panel (the 5-state connection badge with a stale flag, buffered/received/server-drop
captions, auto-scroll/pause/clear/download/reconnect), the connection-error panel, and the
event table (Time/Level/Message/Fields with grep highlighting, field chips, the EmptyState
with a Reconnect affordance, and a bounded auto-scrolling live region), using the P2 tokens +
P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings via the web key names (the translation.liveLogs.* mirror); the
buffered/received/drops captions + the `.txt` download filename interpolate the catalog's
`%1$@` specifiers and are unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift-6
strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0 / iOS 0, exercising the compact branches) over the
real component + token + app-route sources, and by an executed 32-assertion model harness. The
full xcodebuild is BLOCKED only by code-signing (no dev cert) + a pre-existing, repo-wide
Xcode-26.5 `#Preview` toolchain incompatibility in 106 out-of-scope sibling files, with ZERO
diagnostics in any LiveLogs file.

